00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.760
Hello YouTube.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.590
This is CZ speaking.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:11.050
With the release of the new Death Note movie
on Netflix *clear throat* OK I'm not going

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:12.760
to keep up that voice for the entire video.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.660
But anyways, here are The Things You Missed
in Death Note.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.180
The very first episode of Things You Missed
was an episode on the trailer for this movie

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:21.230
and now it's finally been released.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:24.520
One of the biggest complaints I saw about
this movie on Twitter was the lack of the

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.300
iconic potato chip scene.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:30.210
However, it may have actually been referenced
in a small way at a couple different points

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.210
in the film.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:35.230
Mia Sutton is seen eating some potato chips
in Light's room, then he goes over to the

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:37.390
desk and it's covered in crumbs!!

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:40.600
So maybe the scene did take place "off camera"
so to speak.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.190
Did anyone else think when Light got caught
with the homework pages that it was strange

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.510
that she found those, but not the Death Note?

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:50.380
I just imagine her thought process: you may
have this book that's capable of killing 1000s

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:54.690
of people, and that's fine, but boy if you
cheat in my class I will mess you up!

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:58.030
It's even more ridiculous considering that
there have actually been instances of kids

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:01.040
getting in trouble for having fake Death Notes
in schools before.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.239
I attempted to read each page of the Death
Note, but motion blur and Netflix's streaming

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:08.060
quality made it kind of hard, but here's what
I picked up.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:11.330
This page says something about Suicide and
Scarlet Fever.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:14.790
Light Turner is not the first one to have
the Death Note and all the previous pages

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.820
and names are already in there.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:20.390
Some of them were historical figures, others
just seemed to be names.

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:24.470
This guy Jean Chabot was a Canadian legislator
in the 1800s.

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:28.350
Michel Claparede was a French general in the
1700s.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:33.180
Charles Adrien Merode was a nobleman in Europe,
and I believe the name is also French.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:37.200
In fact, it seems that the Death Note spent
quite a lot of time in France.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:42.480
The next page contains Louis Chabot, Michel
Claparede again, with something crossed out,

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:45.200
and Andre Massena, a French Military commander.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:49.630
So I'm thinking one Light's predecessors used
the Death Note as a political weapon in ancient

00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:50.630
France.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:51.930
Can you say spin-off?

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:55.189
Before we continue, I need to set the record
straight on this apple thing.

00:01:55.189 --> 00:01:59.030
For some reason, in this movie, Ryuk does
not, eat the center of the apple.

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:03.079
If you're a Death Note fan, you know that
apple cores are a myth, they don't exist,

00:02:03.079 --> 00:02:04.799
it all just apple.

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:05.720
Don't believe me?

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:06.240
Let me demonstrate.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:21.760
🎵🎵

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:24.830
Another thing I found strange: nobody questions
the destroyed classroom?

00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:28.579
This seems like a bigger deal than helping
some kids cheat on their test, but it never

00:02:28.579 --> 00:02:29.579
comes up again.

00:02:29.579 --> 00:02:34.019
As Light goes to the window, some text reading:
The World, is written on the wall.

00:02:34.019 --> 00:02:38.079
Is that because it's a classroom and classrooms
have maps of the world?

00:02:38.079 --> 00:02:39.079
Yes.

00:02:39.079 --> 00:02:43.090
But could it be a reference to the song title
of the first OP of Death Note?

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:47.500
🎵Hirogaru yami no naka kawashiatta 🎵

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.500
Maybe.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.500
Probably not.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:54.129
In this movie, Light lives with his Dad, so
unfortunately we do not get to see Mrs. Yagami

00:02:54.129 --> 00:02:55.129
or Sayu.

00:02:55.129 --> 00:02:57.379
We actually find out that Light's mom was
killed.

00:02:57.379 --> 00:03:01.199
I had assumed that it was earlier in his life,
but she's still around in this picture on

00:03:01.199 --> 00:03:04.819
Light's 16th birthday, so it must be very
recent.

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:09.329
Now in the anime and manga, the Gods of Death
come from the Shinigami Realm, which is not

00:03:09.329 --> 00:03:10.859
seen any of the films.

00:03:10.859 --> 00:03:13.989
Unless you count the relights, but those are
just the anime cut down into the length of

00:03:13.989 --> 00:03:16.220
a film, so that should not count.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:19.859
Although we don't see the Shinigami Realm
in this movie, that doesn't mean it doesn't

00:03:19.859 --> 00:03:20.859
exist.

00:03:20.859 --> 00:03:25.089
I noticed Rule 65 in the notebook makes reference
to the Shinigami Realm.

00:03:25.089 --> 00:03:28.319
It would also appear that the 19 day rule
is still in effect.

00:03:28.319 --> 00:03:31.599
If you aren't familiar with it, it allows
you to write the cause of death before the

00:03:31.599 --> 00:03:35.329
name, so long as you do fill in the name within
19 days.

00:03:35.329 --> 00:03:40.040
Also, the 490 days you get to to maintain
ownership of the Death Note without possessing

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:45.120
it has been shortened to 7 in this movie,
and for no good reason because it never comes

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.120
up.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:50.050
In this scene Light tries to get Mia to see
Ryuk by having her touch the notebook, which

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:53.239
works in the anime, but not in this movie
apparently.

00:03:53.239 --> 00:03:56.309
So what I'm wondering is, where did he get
the idea to try that?

00:03:56.309 --> 00:03:58.650
Did Light watch the anime or read the manga?

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.489
Do those things exist in the world of this
movie?

00:04:01.489 --> 00:04:02.560
Kind of.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:06.700
The Brode hostage situation takes place in
Little Tokyo in Seattle, which is just a little

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:10.669
reference to Japan, and there a few in this
film, like how Light tries to make it seem

00:04:10.669 --> 00:04:15.579
like he is in Japan by adopting the Kira moniker
(again, did he watch the anime?) and making

00:04:15.579 --> 00:04:17.310
many of his early killings in Japan.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:22.330
We are going to start getting into spoilers
for the anime and the movie now, this is your

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:23.590
final warning.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:28.240
Remember in my initial video how I speculated
that Mia Sutton was the US version of Misa

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.240
Misa?

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:33.539
Well, Mia has an eye on her window, which
is interesting considering that Misa obtains

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:37.330
the Shinigami eyes in the manga, and she is
basically the eyes of Kira.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:42.030
In the movie, there are no Shinigami eyes,
but she does at times play the hand of Kira,

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:44.050
which is what Mikami does in the manga.

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:47.139
The song that Watari sings to L is from the
Wizard of Oz.

00:04:47.139 --> 00:04:49.849
It plays when they skip through the flowers
toward Emerald City.

00:04:49.849 --> 00:04:54.580
I'll talk more about the significance of flowers
in this Death Note movie, later in this video.

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:59.409
Detective Turner has a list of murders that
he suspects to be Kira murders in his office.

00:04:59.409 --> 00:05:03.100
Some of them are kind of funny, and there
are very few heart attacks compared to Light

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:04.100
Yagami.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:05.129
Here are a few examples.

00:05:05.129 --> 00:05:06.770
Eaten by Thylacine.

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:08.000
Attacked by bullshark.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.800
Crushed by crystal chandelier.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:10.800
Falling to death.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.460
Electrocuted while playing guitar in the bath.

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:17.560
There were a few interesting things that L
has, one of which is a golden apple, the other

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:20.199
appears to be a puzzle cube type thing.

00:05:20.199 --> 00:05:25.389
If Mia Sutton is a combination of Misa and
Mikami, maybe L is a combination of L and

00:05:25.389 --> 00:05:26.389
Near.

00:05:26.389 --> 00:05:30.069
The Lind L Taylor scene is skipped over in
favor of L directly confronting Light.

00:05:30.069 --> 00:05:33.659
He claims: "I shall be meeting you face to
face very shortly."

00:05:33.659 --> 00:05:34.819
Which he does.

00:05:34.819 --> 00:05:39.310
In a really short scene, Light notices this
guy following him, who is basically Raye Penber.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:41.789
His name in this movie is Raymond Young.

00:05:41.789 --> 00:05:46.009
In the anime, Light goes on a date with his
classmate Yuri to Spaceworld, which is a Japanese

00:05:46.009 --> 00:05:50.569
amusement park, in an attempt to out the identity
of Raye Penber on the bus.

00:05:50.569 --> 00:05:55.009
In this movie, he takes Mia on a date to this
attraction on Pier 57, where they address

00:05:55.009 --> 00:05:59.610
how the stalker should be dealt with, so I
guess it's supposed to be the same scene.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:01.810
That's not how L holds a phone.

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:03.520
This is how L holds a phone.

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:08.009
It seems strange that some of his other mannerisms
from the anime carried over to Stanfield's

00:06:08.009 --> 00:06:09.169
L, but not this others.

00:06:09.169 --> 00:06:12.849
I guess Watari, is just W's full name in this
movie.

00:06:12.849 --> 00:06:15.409
Light writes "Watari" in the Death Note and
it works.

00:06:15.409 --> 00:06:18.220
In the manga, his real name is Quillish Wammy.

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:20.280
This is probably my favorite entry in the
Death Note.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:24.189
The guy's name is Abdul Aswad, and the cause
of Death.

00:06:24.189 --> 00:06:26.599
Eats a grenade.

00:06:26.599 --> 00:06:27.710
EATS A GRENADE.

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:31.320
At this point, I don't understand why doesn't
Light just burn the page himself?

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.710
That would be the first thing I would do.

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:36.080
If you haven't noticed, this movie is nowhere
near as smart as it's Japanese counterpart.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:40.199
If you haven't seen those movies, I would
highly recommend you check out Death Note

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:41.949
and Death Note II: The Last Name.

00:06:41.949 --> 00:06:45.750
I can't say the same for the spin-off sequel,
L: Change the World.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:47.590
This video is not sponsored.

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:51.900
Both the first and last major Kira killings
happen in front of a florist.

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:55.960
When Mia dies, she lands right in this bed
of flowers, leading me to believe that flowers

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:57.900
are somehow representative of death.

00:06:57.900 --> 00:07:02.219
If flowers are death, than butterflies are
an agent of death, or a spreader of death.

00:07:02.219 --> 00:07:07.860
We see butterflies constantly being associated
with Mia: in her room, in her locker, a butterfly

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:11.860
balloon hovering next to her when she is reunited
with Light close to the end.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:14.779
If you noticed any other references, let me
know in the comments.

